{"items":[{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-bnjuj9nc2ngtmwatnmbqqe","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-bnjuj9nc2ngtmwatnmbqqe","dateCreated":"2025-12-16T17:28:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-19T19:33:16+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Application Recovery Controller (ARC) Region switch allows you to orchestrate the specific steps to switch your multi-Region applications to operate out of another AWS Region and achieve a bounded recovery time in the event of a Regional impairment to your applications. Region switch saves hours of engineering effort and eliminates the operational overhead previously required to complete failover steps, create custom dashboards, and manually gather evidence of a successful recovery for applications across your organization and hosted in multiple AWS accounts. Today, we are announcing three new Region switch capabilities:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cb\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) support\u003c/b\u003e: ARC Region switch is now generally available in AWS GovCloud (US-East and US-West) Regions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cb\u003ePlan execution reports\u003c/b\u003e: Region switch now automatically generates a comprehensive report from each plan execution and saves it to an Amazon S3 bucket of your choice. Each report includes a detailed timeline of events for the recovery operation, resources in scope for the Region switch, alarm states for optional application status alarms, and recovery time objective (RTO) calculations. This eliminates the manual effort previously required to compile evidence and documentation for compliance officers and auditors.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cb\u003eDocumentDB global cluster execution blocks\u003c/b\u003e: Adding to the catalog of 9 execution blocks, Region switch now supports Amazon DocumentDB global cluster execution blocks for automated multi-Region database recovery. This feature allows you to orchestrate DocumentDB global cluster failover and switchover operations within your Region switch plans.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo get started, build a Region switch plan using the ARC console, API, or CLI. See the AWS Regional Services List for availability information. Visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/application-recovery-controller/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehome page\u003c/a\u003e or read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/r53recovery/latest/dg/region-switch.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/12/amazon-application-recovery-controller-region-switch-new-capabilities","postDateTime":"2025-12-19T15:00:00Z","headline":"Amazon Application Recovery Controller region switch now supports three new capabilities"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#application-recovery-controller","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-application-recovery-controller","description":"https://aws.amazon.com/application-recovery-controller/","dateCreated":"2025-09-24T21:15:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-09-24T21:15:43+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-2ry8qh4aehbudbf9bhpo2j","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-2ry8qh4aehbudbf9bhpo2j","dateCreated":"2025-09-18T15:04:00+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-09-24T21:17:34+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eRegion switch in Amazon Application Recovery Controller (ARC) is now available in the Asia Pacific (New Zealand) Region. Region switch allows you to orchestrate the specific steps to operate your cross-AWS account application resources out of another AWS Region. It provides dashboards for real-time visibility into the recovery process and gathers data from across resources and accounts required for reporting to regulators and compliance teams. Region switch supports failover and failback for active/passive multi-Region approaches, and shift-away and return for active/active multi-Region approaches. When you create a Region switch plan, it is replicated to all the Regions your application operates in. This removes dependencies on the Region you are leaving for your recovery.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo get started, build a Region switch plan using the ARC console, API, or CLI. To learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/r53recovery/latest/dg/region-switch.html\"\u003eARC Region switch documentation\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/application-recovery-controller/pricing/\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/09/application-recovery-controller-region-switch-new-zealand/","postDateTime":"2025-09-24T15:03:00Z","headline":"Application Recovery Controller Region switch is now available in Asia Pacific (New Zealand)"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#application-recovery-controller","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-application-recovery-controller","description":"https://aws.amazon.com/application-recovery-controller/","dateCreated":"2025-09-24T21:15:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-09-24T21:15:43+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"}]}],"metadata":{"count":2,"totalHits":2},"fieldTypes":{"regionalAvailability":"LongText","nofollow":"Boolean","date":"Date","language":"Text","title":"Text","postDateTime":"DateTime","body":"Text","postSummary":"LongText","ctaLabel":"Text","mediaThumbnail":"Text","nosnippet":"Boolean","price":"Text","ctaLink":"URL","headline":"Text","contentType":"Text","bodyBack":"LongText","secondaryCTALabel":"Text","primaryCTALink":"URL","noindex":"Boolean","level":"Text","heading":"Text","mediaType":"Text","mediaAlt":"Text","headlineUrl":"Text","mediaSrc":"URL","durationMinutes":"Number","badge":"JSON","videoImageUrl":"URL","postBody":"LongText","secondaryCTALink":"URL","Video":"URL","modifiedDate":"DateTime","namePerson":"Text","location":"Text","time":"Text","publishedDate":"DateTime","durationReadtime":"Number","primaryCTALabel":"Text"}}